Use the Dig UI skill installed at `{{SKILL_DIR}}`.

Start from `SKILL.md`, then load only the references you need:

- Always read `references/global-rules.md`, then `references/global-rules.local.md` when present unless the user explicitly says no global rules.
- Choose one catalog from `references/catalogs/` before writing styles.
- Choose a layout recipe from `references/layouts/` when structuring pages.
- Use `references/tokens.md`, `references/primitives.md`, and `references/checklist.md` as needed.

When implementing or reviewing UI:

- Default to the `dig` catalog unless the page clearly needs another catalog such as `wise` or `apple`.
- Layout defines structure; catalog defines visual language. Do not mix multiple catalogs on one page.
- Prefer tokenized CSS variables over hard-coded colors, radii, and shadows.
- Avoid generic purple SaaS gradients and noisy neon palettes.
